s Karandeep Anand, Disney's newly-appointed chief technology officer]]></title><description>&lt;img border="0" hspace="10" align="left" style="margin-top:3px;margin-right:5px;" src="https://timesofindia.indiatimes.com/photo/134351681.cms" /&gt;<![CDATA[]]></description><link><![CDATA[https://timesofindia.indiatimes.com/world/us/who-is-karandeep-anand-disneys-newly-appointed-chief-technology-officer/articleshow/134351681.cms]]></link><guid><![CDATA[https://timesofindia.indiatimes.com/world/us/who-is-karandeep-anand-disneys-newly-appointed-chief-technology-officer/articleshow/134351681.cms]]></guid><pubDate>2026-09-19T15:31:04+05:30</pubDate><dc:creator xmlns:dc="http://purl.org/dc/elements/1.1/">Gokul Ankari</dc:creator><enclosure type="image/jpeg" url="https://static.toiimg.com/photo/msid-134351723,imgsize-944836.cms"/></item><item><title><![CDATA[Illinois data centre project: $18 billion campus gets first permit as neighbours say they learned about it too late]]></title><description>&lt;img border="0" hspace="10" align="left" style="margin-top:3px;margin-right:5px;" src="https://timesofindia.indiatimes.com/photo/134351461.cms" /&gt;<![CDATA[Grayslake has granted a building permit for a substantial data-centre campus, representing a major advancement in an $18 billion private investment endeavor. Meanwhile, community members are voicing worries about lack of input and possible environmental repercussions. The developer is committed to thorough community engagement and meeting regulatory guidelines. Site work will be executed in phases, with initial construction about to kick off shortly.]]></description><link><![CDATA[https://timesofindia.indiatimes.com/world/us/illinois-issued-the-first-permit-for-an-18-billion-data-centre-campus-covering-up-to-472-acres-an-800000-sq-ft-first-building-moves-ahead-as-neighbours-say-they-learned-too-late-to-weigh-in/articleshow/134351461.cms]]></link><guid><![CDATA[https://timesofindia.indiatimes.com/world/us/illinois-issued-the-first-permit-for-an-18-billion-data-centre-campus-covering-up-to-472-acres-an-800000-sq-ft-first-building-moves-ahead-as-neighbours-say-they-learned-too-late-to-weigh-in/articleshow/134351461.cms]]></guid><pubDate>2026-09-19T16:00:00+05:30</pubDate><dc:creator xmlns:dc="http://purl.org/dc/elements/1.1/">TOI World Desk</dc:creator><enclosure type="image/jpeg" url="https://static.toiimg.com/photo/msid-134351483,imgsize-1170726.cms"/></item><item><title><![CDATA[MIT robot builds working laser cavity in 50 maneuvers under 30 minutes, self-corrects after disruption]]></title><description>&lt;img border="0" hspace="10" align="left" style="margin-top:3px;margin-right:5px;" src="https://timesofindia.indiatimes.com/photo/134351299.cms" /&gt;<![CDATA[Massachusetts Institute of Technology researchers developed a robotic optics laboratory.  This system autonomously assembles and aligns laser cavities with precision.  The robot can also correct experimental setups after they are disturbed.  This technology could accelerate testing for various optical devices and materials.  Future applications envision remote interaction with these automated research environments.]]></description><link><![CDATA[https://timesofindia.indiatimes.com/science/discovery/mits-robotic-optics-lab-built-a-working-laser-cavity-in-50-maneuvers-and-under-30-minutes-when-researchers-moved-components-it-realigned-them-automatically-with-micron-scale-precision/articleshow/134351299.cms]]></link><guid><![CDATA[https://timesofindia.indiatimes.com/science/discovery/mits-robotic-optics-lab-built-a-working-laser-cavity-in-50-maneuvers-and-under-30-minutes-when-researchers-moved-components-it-realigned-them-automatically-with-micron-scale-precision/articleshow/134351299.cms]]></guid><pubDate>2026-09-19T16:00:00+05:30</pubDate><dc:creator xmlns:dc="http://purl.org/dc/elements/1.1/">TOI Science Desk</dc:creator><enclosure type="image/jpeg" url="https://static.toiimg.com/photo/msid-134351389,imgsize-2076787.cms"/></item><item><title><![CDATA[In 1927, Henry Ford built a town over a stretch of Amazon rainforest; in 1945 he was forced to sell it for $250,000]]></title><description>&lt;img border="0" hspace="10" align="left" style="margin-top:3px;margin-right:5px;" src="https://timesofindia.indiatimes.com/photo/134350941.cms" /&gt;<![CDATA[Henry Ford initiated the Fordlandia project in the lush Amazon rainforest of Brazil to secure a steady rubber supply. However, his corporate methods often clashed with local traditions and agricultural practices. The plantation faced numerous obstacles, including pests and diseases harming the rubber trees. Despite investing heavily over seventeen years, Fordlandia ultimately succumbed to failure, illustrating the challenges of integrating foreign business models within local ecosystems.]]></description><link><![CDATA[https://timesofindia.indiatimes.com/world/us/in-1927-henry-ford-took-over-a-stretch-of-the-amazon-rainforest-to-build-an-american-town-inside-it-in-1945-he-was-forced-to-sell-it-for-250000/articleshow/134350941.cms]]></link><guid><![CDATA[https://timesofindia.indiatimes.com/world/us/in-1927-henry-ford-took-over-a-stretch-of-the-amazon-rainforest-to-build-an-american-town-inside-it-in-1945-he-was-forced-to-sell-it-for-250000/articleshow/134350941.cms]]></guid><pubDate>2026-09-19T15:03:09+05:30</pubDate><dc:creator xmlns:dc="http://purl.org/dc/elements/1.1/">TOI World Desk</dc:creator><enclosure type="image/jpeg" url="https://static.toiimg.com/photo/msid-134351002,imgsize-945404.cms"/></item><item><title><![CDATA[Ellen DeGeneres’ $6.7M farmhouse is back on the market for $14.75M after 7 years]]></title><description>&lt;img border="0" hspace="10" align="left" style="margin-top:3px;margin-right:5px;" src="https://timesofindia.indiatimes.com/photo/134350897.cms" /&gt;<![CDATA[]]></description><link><![CDATA[https://timesofindia.indiatimes.com/real-estate/news/ellen-degeneres-and-portia-de-rossi-paid-6-7-million-for-a-1917-santa-barbara-farmhouse-in-2018-spent-a-year-restoring-it-sold-it-in-2019-and-its-now-relisted-for-14-75-million/articleshow/134350897.cms]]></link><guid><![CDATA[https://timesofindia.indiatimes.com/real-estate/news/ellen-degeneres-and-portia-de-rossi-paid-6-7-million-for-a-1917-santa-barbara-farmhouse-in-2018-spent-a-year-restoring-it-sold-it-in-2019-and-its-now-relisted-for-14-75-million/articleshow/134350897.cms]]></guid><pubDate>2026-09-19T14:28:11+05:30</pubDate><dc:creator xmlns:dc="http://purl.org/dc/elements/1.1/">TOI Real Estate Desk</dc:creator><enclosure type="image/jpeg" url="https://static.toiimg.com/photo/msid-134350962,imgsize-117730.cms"/></item><item><title><![CDATA[California buried a gas pipeline and removed its final barrier; salmon returned after 70 years]]></title><description>&lt;img border="0" hspace="10" align="left" style="margin-top:3px;margin-right:5px;" src="https://timesofindia.indiatimes.com/photo/134350679.cms" /&gt;<![CDATA[A decades-long barrier blocking fish migration in Alameda Creek was removed in 2025.  This action reopened over twenty miles of upstream habitat for migratory fish.  Chinook salmon were documented in the newly accessible area shortly after the construction.  This marked the first access to this watershed section since the 1950s.  The project is part of a larger, nearly thirty-year restoration effort.]]></description><link><![CDATA[https://timesofindia.indiatimes.com/science/nature/in-2025-california-buried-a-gas-pipeline-20-feet-below-alameda-creek-and-removed-its-final-8-foot-barrier-that-same-week-chinook-salmon-reached-this-part-of-the-watershed-for-the-first-time-since-the-1950s/articleshow/134350679.cms]]></link><guid><![CDATA[https://timesofindia.indiatimes.com/science/nature/in-2025-california-buried-a-gas-pipeline-20-feet-below-alameda-creek-and-removed-its-final-8-foot-barrier-that-same-week-chinook-salmon-reached-this-part-of-the-watershed-for-the-first-time-since-the-1950s/articleshow/134350679.cms]]></guid><pubDate>2026-09-19T15:00:00+05:30</pubDate><dc:creator xmlns:dc="http://purl.org/dc/elements/1.1/">TOI Science Desk</dc:creator><enclosure type="image/jpeg" url="https://static.toiimg.com/photo/msid-134350788,imgsize-2494723.cms"/></item></channel></rss>